{"kind":"artifact","text":"spike/cmd/gitseq-report at 31ddeb38f8449f88bb9f8d2422572045a527fb20 on request/spike-evidence.\n\nA red run now says which of two different things happened. Only a test that actually reported failure makes the run a fail; a test that was skipped, never appeared, or whose runner died leaves the property unestablished and makes the run an error, which is a harness defect rather than a security regression. If both occurred the security finding outranks the runner complaint. Both exit non-zero, so CI stays red either way; what changes is what the reader is told, in the printed headline and in the written evidence.\n\nThe evidence for a failing CI run stopped being discarded. .github/workflows/ci.yml uploads spike/.spike/ on failure with a thirty-day retention, chosen because these files describe adversarial cases: long enough to compare a repeat against its predecessor, not indefinite on a public runner.\n\nOn the intermittent the request asked to diagnose. Its cause is identifiable and was already fixed on main before this branch started. Before merge c9dc187d the runner executed the whole repository suite, so any unrelated flaky test set runErr and printed fail while all six adversarial cases carried pass. Five of five failing CI runs I checked were this step, each printing nothing but the word and no test output at all. Every CI run since that merge is green, as were ten consecutive local runs at current main. Which test failed in those runs cannot be recovered, because the evidence was written to a file and deleted with the runner — the defect this head closes. I am reporting the cause as named and already fixed rather than claiming to have fixed it.\n\nBoth failure modes were forced separately through the real command and their output read, rather than inferred from one run. A passing run writes a byte-identical tracked SPIKE-RESULTS.md. go vet and the full suite pass, and the worktree is clean at this head.","body":{"branch":"request/spike-evidence","commit":"31ddeb38f8449f88bb9f8d2422572045a527fb20","head":"31ddeb38f8449f88bb9f8d2422572045a527fb20","path":"spike/cmd/gitseq-report"}}